# Only three things stay out of this repository, and each for a reason that is
# not "it is big": committing it would be wrong, not merely wasteful.

# A virtualenv is machine-specific. It holds compiled binaries and absolute
# paths from whoever created it, so a committed one is broken for everyone else.
# `uv sync --extra dev` rebuilds it from uv.lock in seconds -- see the README.
.venv/

# Generated from the source beside it, and regenerated whenever Python feels
# like it. Committing it means a diff every time someone runs the tests.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Per-machine, by design: `.claude/settings.local.json` is the local override of
# the shared `.claude/settings.json`, which IS committed. Secrets and personal
# paths belong here, which is exactly why it does not travel.
.claude/settings.local.json

# macOS.
.DS_Store
